<figure class="art-fig art-fig--pair">
<div class="art-fig__grid">
<svg viewBox="0 0 480 490" role="img" aria-label="On-premises Travel Rule software" aria-describedby="f3-d" font-family="inherit"><desc id="f3-d">The Travel Rule software and the records with personal data both sit inside the CASP's own infrastructure. The software provider only sends updates, which the CASP installs. Travel Rule messages go out to counterparty VASPs. The CASP runs hosting, access control, patching, backups and monitoring.</desc><defs><marker id="f3-a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z" fill="var(--muted)"/></marker></defs><text x="16" y="30" font-size="22" font-weight="700" fill="var(--ink)">On-premises (self-hosted)</text><rect x="16" y="50" width="200" height="52" rx="12" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="116.0" y="82.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Software provider</text><path d="M116 102 L116 146" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="5 4" marker-end="url(#f3-a)"/><text x="130" y="130.0" font-size="15" fill="var(--muted)">updates, installed by the CASP</text><rect x="16" y="150" width="448" height="168" rx="18" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/><text x="32" y="178" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="var(--accent)">CASP's own infrastructure</text><rect x="32" y="194" width="200" height="104" rx="12" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="132.0" y="240.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Travel Rule</text><text x="132.0" y="264.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">software</text><rect x="248" y="194" width="200" height="104" rx="12" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="348.0" y="240.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Records and</text><text x="348.0" y="264.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">personal data</text><path d="M240 318 L240 360" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#f3-a)"/><text x="254" y="345.0" font-size="15" fill="var(--muted)">Travel Rule messages</text><rect x="130" y="364" width="220" height="50" rx="12" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="240.0" y="395.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Counterparty VASPs</text><text x="16" y="452" font-size="16" fill="var(--body)">The CASP runs hosting, access control,</text><text x="16" y="474" font-size="16" fill="var(--body)">patching, backups and monitoring.</text></svg>
<svg viewBox="0 0 480 584" role="img" aria-label="SaaS Travel Rule software" aria-describedby="f4-d" font-family="inherit"><desc id="f4-d">The CASP's compliance team uses the service through a web app or API. The Travel Rule software, the records with personal data, provider staff access, and the hosting provider and other subcontractors all sit in the provider's cloud. Travel Rule messages go out to counterparty VASPs from there. The provider runs the service, while the CASP stays accountable and oversees the provider.</desc><defs><marker id="f4-a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z" fill="var(--muted)"/></marker></defs><text x="16" y="30" font-size="22" font-weight="700" fill="var(--ink)">SaaS (provider-hosted)</text><rect x="16" y="50" width="220" height="52" rx="12" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="126.0" y="82.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">CASP compliance team</text><path d="M126 102 L126 146" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#f4-a)"/><text x="140" y="130.0" font-size="15" fill="var(--muted)">web app or API</text><rect x="16" y="150" width="448" height="262" rx="18" fill="var(--surface-sunk)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" stroke-width="2"/><text x="32" y="178" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="var(--ink)">Provider's cloud</text><rect x="32" y="194" width="200" height="96" rx="12" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="132.0" y="236.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Travel Rule</text><text x="132.0" y="260.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">software</text><rect x="248" y="194" width="200" height="96" rx="12" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="348.0" y="236.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Records and</text><text x="348.0" y="260.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">personal data</text><rect x="32" y="302" width="200" height="96" rx="12" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="132.0" y="344.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Provider staff</text><text x="132.0" y="368.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">access</text><rect x="248" y="302" width="200" height="96" rx="12" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="6 5"/><text x="348.0" y="344.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Hosting and</text><text x="348.0" y="368.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">subcontractors</text><path d="M240 412 L240 454" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#f4-a)"/><text x="254" y="439.0" font-size="15" fill="var(--muted)">Travel Rule messages</text><rect x="130" y="458" width="220" height="50" rx="12" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="240.0" y="489.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Counterparty VASPs</text><text x="16" y="546" font-size="16" fill="var(--body)">The provider runs the service. The CASP</text><text x="16" y="568" font-size="16" fill="var(--body)">stays accountable and oversees the provider.</text></svg>
</div>
<figcaption>Where Travel Rule data sits in each model. The deployment changes who runs what; it does not move regulatory accountability away from the CASP.</figcaption>
</figure>
